index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..aa9ad0cdec82c02656a99837b86e2e67ab0804ac
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,210 @@
+# Exact tensor dependences from arXiv 1303.6914
+
+| profile | value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B — no-tool compression** |
+| native domain | algebra |
+| object regime | rational exact |
+| computational core | linear algebra |
+| certificate form | rational vector |
+| intuition | invariant: one finite difference kills every coordinate polynomial |
+| domain essentiality | native |
+| reduction | none |
+
+**Release status:** every local gate G1–G9(c) passes, but the required oracle
+evidence is externally blocked. All bare, structural-hint, and placebo calls
+returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded`; none is scored as a model
+failure. The family must not be submitted as hardened until those three runs
+obtain real responses.
+
+## Problem and construction
+
+Chiantini, Mella, and Ottaviani's [*One example of general unidentifiable
+tensors*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.6914) proves in Theorem 3.5 that a general
+rank-eight tensor in `C^3 tensor C^6 tensor C^6` has at least six decompositions
+into eight simple tensors. Definition 2.1 fixes “identifiable” as uniqueness of
+such a decomposition. Lemmas 3.2–3.3 put the eight points on a special
+Segre-Veronese fourfold and use the ancillary Macaulay2 calculation to establish
+the six-point fibre; Remark 3.7 says that the exact number of decompositions is
+not known.
+
+This generator hands the solver `2n+4` simple tensors over `Q`, each specified
+by three polynomial factor vectors and exact integer change-of-basis matrices.
+The requested witness is a bounded vector of nonzero, pairwise-distinct rational
+coefficients whose weighted tensor sum is zero. Verification substitutes the
+coefficients and checks every resulting polynomial moment with integers. It
+accepts any valid bounded dependence and never reads the planted answer.
+
+Generation composes an identity rather than solving the finished instance. The
+factor exponents are selected so every tensor coordinate is a polynomial in its
+displayed node of degree at most `2n+2`. There are `2n+4` equally spaced nodes,
+so signed finite-difference coefficients annihilate every coordinate at once.
+Random unimodular basis changes preserve the identity. At the paper-matching
+`n=6` preset, the positive and negative coefficients each support eight terms,
+giving two exact eight-term decompositions in `Q^3 tensor Q^6 tensor Q^6`.
+
+## Why Track B
+
+This is not a Track A claim. The presented task is linear dependence, so a
+specialist flattens the tensors into a `3n^2` by `2n+4` matrix and performs exact
+nullspace elimination. The implemented reference algorithm uses arithmetic
+modulo the prime `2^61-1`; unimodularity and the Vandermonde construction make
+this exact for the generated regime. It runs in `O(n^4)` field operations and
+solved 8/8 shipping instances. At `n=24` its median measured cost was
+**1,719,617 operations and 0.193 s**.
+
+The compact route notices that every flattened coordinate is a low-degree
+polynomial of the node. Sorting the nodes and generating row `2n+3` of Pascal's
+triangle by its recurrence takes **102 exact arithmetic operations** at shipping
+size. That is short enough in context, while a 1.7-million-operation dense
+elimination is not. The paper's own route is different and more geometric: its
+certificate of generic non-identifiability comes from the Macaulay2 fibre
+calculation in Lemma 3.3, not from this finite-difference special family.
+
+## Worked demo (`seed=0`)
+
+This is the complete rendered demo:
+
+```text
+Exact dependence among simple tensors
+
+All arithmetic is over the rational numbers Q.  For a list of exponents E and
+an integer t, define phi_E(t) to be the column vector [t^e for e in E], in the
+displayed exponent order.  Ordinary matrix-vector multiplication is used.
+
+Let
+  E_A = [0,1,2]
+  E_B = [0,1,2]
+  E_C = [0,3,4]
+and let the three integer matrices be
+  M_A = [[1,0,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,1]]
+  M_B = [[1,0,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,1]]
+  M_C = [[1,0,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,1]]
+
+For each displayed parameter t_i below, form
+  a_i = M_A phi_E_A(t_i) in Q^3,
+  b_i = M_B phi_E_B(t_i) in Q^3,
+  c_i = M_C phi_E_C(t_i) in Q^3,
+and the simple tensor T_i = a_i tensor b_i tensor c_i.  Its (r,s,u)
+coordinate is exactly a_i[r]*b_i[s]*c_i[u].  Indices i,r,s,u are all 0-based.
+
+The 10 parameters, in tensor-index order i=0,...,9, are
+  t = [1,9,7,3,5,6,4,2,10,8]
+
+Find exactly 10 pairwise-distinct nonzero rational coefficients lambda_i such
+that
+  sum_i lambda_i T_i = 0
+in Q^3 tensor Q^3 tensor Q^3.  A rational is encoded as [p,q], meaning the
+reduced fraction p/q, with q>0.  Every coefficient must satisfy
+|p| <= 126 and 1 <= q <= 7.
+Order matters: coefficient i multiplies the displayed tensor T_i.  Repeated or
+zero coefficients are forbidden.  Any vector satisfying these conditions is
+accepted.  Positive and negative terms may equivalently be moved to opposite
+sides, giving two decompositions of one tensor into simple tensors.
+
+Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags as one JSON list of exactly
+10 rational pairs [[p_0,q_0],...,[p_9,q_9]].
+Example format: <answer>[[1,1],[-3,1],[3,1],[-1,1]]</answer>
+Whitespace inside the tags is allowed. Output nothing else inside the tags.
+```
+
+The answer is
+`[[1,1],[9,1],[84,1],[36,1],[126,1],[-126,1],[-84,1],[-9,1],[-1,1],[-36,1]]`.
+`verify` returns `(True, "ok")`; dropping the last pair returns
+`(False, "expected 10 coefficients, received 9")`. A person can solve this
+smallest preset on paper by sorting the ten nodes and writing the signed ninth
+finite-difference row.
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| preset | n | terms | flattened rows | answer chars | scalar atoms | compact ops | status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 3 | 10 | 27 | 74 | 20 | 18 | hand example |
+| easy | 6 | 16 | 108 | 139 | 32 | 30 | exact paper dimensions |
+| medium | 14 | 32 | 588 | 379 | 64 | 62 | local gates pass |
+| hard | 24 | 52 | 1,728 | 841 | 104 | 102 | **shipping preset; oracle blocked** |
+
+`escalate()` first increases mixing rounds and coefficient height while the
+answer length stays fixed. Only after exhausting those axes does it increase
+`n`; it returns `"cap_bound"` before any answer or operation cap is crossed.
+
+## Gate results
+
+| gate | result | measured evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 12/12 preset-seed plants verify; 12/12 JSON round trips |
+| G2 | pass | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | fenced prose round-trip succeeds; garbage returns `None` |
+| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 structure-aware bounded rational guesses |
+| G5 | pass | shipping density estimate 0/200,000; reference median 1,719,617 ops / 0.193 s |
+| G6 | pass | four attacks × 8 seeds, 0 successes; reference and compact routes both 8/8 |
+| G7 | pass | `n=24` to `n=48`, rows 1,728 to 6,912; doubled plant verifies |
+| G8 | pass | 100/100 invariance and carried-witness checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | pass | 841 chars, 211 estimated tokens, 104 scalar atoms, 102 operations |
+
+The failing attacks are factor-height outlier ranking, greedy cancellation of
+only the degree-zero moment, 256 bounded random restarts, and the in-context
+alternating-linear ansatz. The successful standard algorithm is correctly
+reported separately as `reference_algorithm` for Track B.
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+
+These are API errors, not unsolved model attempts:
+
+| arm | preset | model(s) drawn | seeds | scored | result |
+|---|---|---|---|---:|---|
+| bare | easy | Grok 4.6; Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview ×3 | 465993200, 1702745206, 1745487587, 921619732 | 0 | four HTTP 403 quota errors |
+| structural | hard | Grok 4.6 ×2; Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview ×2 | 733815406, 91622052, 1181855595, 860350361 | 0 | four HTTP 403 quota errors |
+| placebo | hard | GPT-5.6 Terra; Claude Sonnet 5 ×3 | 199343755, 63517745, 437283882, 1096637368 | 0 | four HTTP 403 quota errors |
+
+| G9 arm | solved / scored attempts | conclusion |
+|---|---:|---|
+| bare | 0 / 0 | not estimable |
+| hinted | 0 / 0 | not estimable; `hinted_verdict="not_run"` |
+| placebo | 0 / 0 | not estimable |
+
+`hinted - placebo` is undefined. The structural hint's effect on the claimed
+invariant cannot be inferred from quota failures.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+import json
+import gen_1303_6914 as g
+
+inst = g.make_instance(seed=7, **g.DIFFICULTY[g.SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY])
+statement = g.render(inst)
+reply = "<answer>" + json.dumps(inst["answer"]) + "</answer>"
+candidate = g.parse_answer(reply)
+assert g.verify(inst, candidate) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+After restoring OpenRouter quota, rerun the bare loop here and the hinted and
+placebo loops in their existing scratch directories. To emit examples from the
+repository root:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 1303.6914 20
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+- This is a rational special family in the paper's native tensor language, not
+  a sampler of the paper's *general* complex tensors. At `n=6` it certifies two
+  eight-term expressions; it does not reproduce the paper's lower bound of six
+  decompositions, and it does not prove that the common tensor has minimal rank
+  eight. Those claims are deliberately absent from the statement and checker.
+- G4 samples uniformly from the declared finite language of pairwise-distinct,
+  nonzero reduced rationals within the printed bounds. Its 0/200,000 result
+  measures only that prior; it does not model a solver that recognizes finite
+  differences or another structured ansatz.
+- The generic exact reference algorithm already solves every instance, which is
+  why this is Track B. Gröbner-basis and homotopy-continuation attacks were not
+  run; they would add cost without changing that conclusion. No numerical ALS
+  attack was tested because the requested witness is exact.
+- `canonical_key` is exact for generated column permutations, swapping the two
+  equal-dimensional modes, arbitrary unimodular mode-basis changes, and common
+  scaling of all nodes. It is not a complete invariant for arbitrary projective
+  equivalence of tensor point configurations.
+- Most importantly, no oracle call was scored. The transcript files establish
+  an external quota blocker only, not LLM hardness.
