The sampler is now genuinely structure-aware: every random candidate has the required shape, bounds, distinctness, negation pairing, and therefore the freely deducible degree-zero cancellation. I also tightened G5 from a zero-hit estimate to an exact count: the Vandermonde kernel is one-dimensional, so all bounded witnesses are scalar multiples of the finite-difference row (26 at the shipping preset).
