- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6914/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The generator constructs two exact eight-term decompositions in \(\mathbb Q^3\otimes\mathbb Q^6\otimes\mathbb Q^6\) using a paired-root barycentric identity. All local gates pass:

- Guessing: 0/200,000; exactly 2 valid bounded witnesses.
- Reference algorithm: 12,837 rational operations, approximately 0.026 seconds.
- Compact route: 136 exact operations.
- Four adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Worst measured answer: 951 characters, 238 estimated tokens, 32 atoms.

It is not yet submission-ready: OpenRouter exhausted its quota, so all final bare/hinted/placebo calls returned HTTP 403 and produced zero scored attempts. The transcripts record that external blocker without treating it as model failure.
