Completed a native algebraic Track B generator based on the paper’s tensor-decomposition setting.

Key results:

- All 9 gates pass.
- Shipping preset: `medium`, with 16 rank-one tensors in \(\mathbb Q^3\otimes\mathbb Q^6\otimes\mathbb Q^6\).
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Reference elimination: 12,837 operations; compact barycentric route: 136 operations.
- Oracle loop: `easy` solved 3/3; `medium` held 0/3.
- G9: bare, structural, and placebo arms each held 0/3.
- Maximum answer: 696 characters, approximately 174 tokens, 32 atoms.
- Direct tensor-coordinate equality independently verified across eight shipping seeds.
- End-to-end emission successfully produced two profiled JSONL instances.

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6914/gen_1303_6914.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6914/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6914/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6914/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6914/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6914/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The construction uses an even-polynomial barycentric identity to manufacture an exact dependence among sixteen simple tensors, yielding two eight-term decompositions. It remains honest about differing from the paper’s existential generic result in Theorem 3.5. [Paper on arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.6914).
